From 76d6295621b712d7f478d307896f28412b30b75f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Steiner <tomac@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:16:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] [iOS] Serve Blink's built-in AI APIs from the on-device
 models

With `use_blink`, Blink has the built-in AI APIs itself and asks the
browser for a `blink::mojom::AIManager`. iOS now answers with one backed
by the same engine as the WebKit build: Apple Foundation Models where
the device has Apple Intelligence, Gemma 4 otherwise. It serves
`LanguageModel` so far, and keeps each session's conversation, since the
engine takes the whole conversation every turn. `ios-built-in-ai-apis`
turns the Blink features on, which are off on iOS.

`ios_blink_single_process` runs Blink in the app's process without JIT,
as on tvOS, and leaves out the BrowserEngineKit extensions, so the app
needs none of the browser engine entitlements. `--remote-debugging-port`
serves DevTools, as content_shell does. The build gets an icon of its
own, with a segment of the Chromium logo.
